# Atlas Sphere — a 40x84 grid of dots drawn with one Skia Atlas; touching the canvas
# springs a progress value and every RSXform is rewritten each frame so dots near the
# finger stay large and pull toward it (a "sphere" lens), far ones collapse.
# What this test covers: a tap (begin + immediate touches-up), a long press in
# place, slow pans across the whole canvas through the corners and edges
# (dots hidden/unhidden as the lens moves), a pan that leaves the canvas,
# fast repeated touches that reverse the 600ms/1000ms springs mid-flight,
# and a final release so the grid settles back.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/atlas-sphere"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
wait 1500
press 200 470
wait 1200
longpress 200 470 1500
wait 1200
# Corners and edges.
gesture pan 50 145 300 0 1200
wait 300
gesture pan 310 160 0 630 1500
wait 300
gesture pan 310 790 -260 0 1200
wait 300
gesture pan 50 795 0 -650 1500
wait 300
# Diagonal through the centre and out of the canvas.
gesture pan 60 160 280 620 1500
wait 1200
gesture pan 200 470 190 380 800
wait 1200
# Fast repeated touches, reversing the springs.
press 120 300
wait 150
press 280 650
wait 150
press 200 470 --count 4
wait 300
gesture pan 100 400 200 0 200
wait 100
gesture pan 300 500 -200 0 200
wait 1500
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\" id=\"xmark\""
wait 1500
